      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "oasis",
            "ref": "v-oasis"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the desert and the paintings in the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "grottoes",
            "zh": "洞窟"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "... if you’ve been to Dunhuang, you must know them well. People have shown interest in this historic town for thousands of years. But when we talk about it today, it’s hard not to mention the “Daughter of Dunhuang”—Fan Jinshi."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Fan grew up in Shanghai. While studying at Peking University, she found her love for "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "archaeology"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This love led her to Dunhuang. After graduation, she was sent to work there. The ancient "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "relics",
            "ref": "v-relic"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "amazed",
            "ref": "v-amaze"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Fan. She decided to protect them as well as she could."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Life in Dunhuang was hard. The tables, chairs, and beds were all made of "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "mud",
            "ref": "v-mud"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The roof was made of paper. But nothing could kill Fan’s love for that place."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Over the past 60 years, Fan has walked through the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Mogao Caves",
            "zh": "莫高窟"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " many times. She has carefully studied every painting and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "sculpture",
            "ref": "v-sculpture"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Fan planned and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "carried out",
            "ref": "v-carry-out"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the largest protection program in the history of the Mogao Caves. She put forward the idea of building a “"
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "digital",
            "ref": "v-digital"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Dunhuang” and has also helped to organize many successful exhibitions of local arts. “During the day, I think about Dunhuang. At night, I dream about it. As long as I’m alive, I will try to protect it,” she once said."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Fan hopes that more young people will become interested in Dunhuang. She hopes its relics will always be carefully protected."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
